PyroWave

Windows builds with PyroWave support ship libpyrowave-shared-1.dll, built from
https://github.com/Themaister/pyrowave together with the parts of Granite
(https://github.com/Themaister/Granite) and volk (https://github.com/zeux/volk) it
links. All three are MIT licensed; their license texts are installed under
licenses/pyrowave next to the application. The SDK is built with the patches in
rust/codec-patches/pyrowave, three of them adapted from Punktfunk
(https://git.unom.io/unom/punktfunk, Copyright (c) 2026 unom - Enrico Bühler,
MIT OR Apache-2.0, used under MIT); the MIT notice is in rust/THIRD_PARTY.md.

Foundation Sunshine

The AMD encoder's opt-in treatment of the low-latency mode, the input queue size
and the AV1 encoding latency mode (rust/core/src/encoder_policy.rs), and the
reasoning behind it, are derived from Foundation Sunshine: AlkaidLab/foundation-sunshine
commit 3340d28 ("feat(amf): align AMD aggressive defaults with FFmpeg amfenc",
AlkaidLab/foundation-sunshine#666) by qiin2333. Both projects are licensed under GPLv3.

InputPlumber and SDL

The virtual Steam Deck controller (rust/core/src/steam_deck.rs) uses the Steam Deck's
HID report descriptors and the feature-report replies Steam expects as captured by
InputPlumber (https://github.com/ShadowBlip/InputPlumber, GPLv3), and the input
report layout and button bits from SDL's SDL_hidapi_steamdeck.c and
controller_structs.h (https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL, zlib license).

Composite DualSense haptics

The Rust composite DualSense implementation was adapted for Rubylight on
2026-10-13 from Nonary/Vibepollo commit 8b3ea1c4a41c383752475ffa551168a16b024d48
(GPL-3.0-or-later), and USB reports/calibration from Nonary/libvirtualgamepad
commit 9edbce11ad71e9455867c356c8368a6b39fa2242 (MIT, Copyright 2026 Chase Payne).
Composite descriptors use HIDMaestro's MIT profile, Copyright 2026 HIDMaestro
Contributors. Original notices remain in rust/core/src/dualsense/descriptors.rs;
the complete MIT terms are also included in rust/THIRD_PARTY.md.

